-- want-one-fs-windows-v040.txt --
swath: staying on one filesystem needs each directory's device, which this platform's engine does not read
-- want-work-dir.txt --
swath: --work-dir is the work directory of a dataset in a bucket; a dataset directory is its own
See 'swath list --help'.
-- want-inode-limit.txt --
swath: the tree has more than 1 file with several hard links, which swath du counts once each: run it again with -l to count every name, or with --max-inodes N to remember more of them (about 100 MB a million)
